<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Messenians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Messenians were the people of Messenia in the south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. Conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> in the 8th and 7th centuries BCE, most were reduced to helots and rebelled repeatedly, while refugees settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafpaktos">Naupactus</a> and at Zancle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, renamed Messana. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> defeated Sparta at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a> freed Messenia and founded the city of Messene in 369 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/messenians.jpg" alt="Messenians" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peulle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palace_of_Nestor_mausoleum_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
